      "writtenOn": "2022-01-13T01:09:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Having kError \u003d 0 and its value increase for labels that are arguably of lower priority threw me for a loop. I suppose it is inline with bug priorities, where p0 is highest.\n\nThat being said, I think SKGPU_MAX_PRIORITY is more understandable as SKGPU_MIN_PRIORITY, since it is the lowest priority that is logged. It\u0027s then an implementation detail that we use \u0027\u003c\u003d\u0027 for performing that test.\n \nwdyt?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 24,
        "startChar": 42,
        "endLine": 24,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "15a23bd827bc99f7d71cb53669c42a704e529234",
